WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.376
- [Speaker] Launch, launch, launch.

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:03.840
(drone engine firing)

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.030
- [Narrator] This is
the new Valkyrie drone.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.950
It's a prototype of a system that is said

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.490
to take out targets over a
distance of up to 3,000 miles

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.980
and run on artificial intelligence.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.070
The Valkyrie XQ-58A could
be an important part

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:20.010
of the US military's
multi-billion dollar effort

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:22.620
to expand its arsenal
with thousands of drones

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:24.180
in the next several years.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.630
All so it can keep up with
increasingly advanced adversaries

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:28.650
like China.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.570
- The Department of Defense
has been quite clear

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.650
that there's a concern

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.200
about the conventional military
balance really shifting

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.510
in the Indo-Pacific in favor of China,

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:37.920
which has more missiles

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.840
and more people than the United States.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.900
And so to offset that
eroding conventional balance,

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.340
there's a view that we need to buy

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.580
more next generation drones
to bring mass to the theater

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.980
and reset the regional balance.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.110
- [Narrator] Here's how the
Valkyrie is built for stealth,

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.720
and how it could fit into
the US military's plans

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.080
to establish a fleet of
artificial intelligence systems.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.030
- It's really the only system flying,

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.095
particularly that's been
flying as long as it has,

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:05.460
with mission configuration
systems, with autonomy,

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.350
with artificial intelligence,

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:10.260
that's in the true attritable class range,

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.510
which means sub-$10 million,

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.340
fully integrated, mission capable.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.740
- [Narrator] The Valkyrie, made
by defense company, Kratos,

00:01:16.740 --> 00:01:18.510
is designed for stealth missions

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.850
using parts that are easily sourced.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.710
It is still in the development process

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.440
and will have to compete
with other AI-equipped drones

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.330
for additional military funding.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.710
But within its class of drones,

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.410
around the five to $10
million price point,

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:34.440
military experts say
it's a notable contender.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.810
- We focus on a reduced number of parts.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:38.250
Obviously the fewer parts you have,

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.050
typically the less expensive something is.

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.090
Some of the avionics are common

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.100
with general aviation aircraft.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.670
Some of the avionics are
custom and designed by us

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.270
and by some of our suppliers
specifically for the Valkyrie.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.930
It's the mix of all those that
allows you to have a system

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:57.360
with the capability level that this has,

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:59.091
but without the sticker price

00:01:59.091 --> 00:02:02.400
of what typically would be
a manned fighter aircraft.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.830
- [Narrator] The Valkyrie
weighs 2,500 pounds,

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:07.920
about as much as two or
three concert grand pianos.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.740
30 feet long with a wingspan of 27 feet,

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.980
it's made to evade radar
detection through its curved shape

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.950
and more specific features
like the serpentine inlet

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.170
that feeds its turbofan engine.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.260
The Valkyrie can accelerate to Mach 0.85,

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.220
travel 3,000 miles at up
to 45,000 feet in altitude,

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.100
and carry 600 pounds of weapons internally

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.930
and the same amount on each wing.

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.930
And it doesn't require a runway to launch.

00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:37.440
It can fly from aircraft
carriers, or small air fields.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.930
But one of the most important
parts of the Valkyrie

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.310
is what's controlling it.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:44.400
- It's a combination of
the AI with the features

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.680
of the aircraft itself
that really make it unique.

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.660
So think about the Vanguard programs

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.467
that the Air Force has rolled out to say,

00:02:50.467 --> 00:02:51.870
"This represents the future."

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.120
Like adding un-crewed systems,

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.920
performing manned, unmanned teaming,

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.083
performing multiple teams of
un-crewed aircraft together,

00:03:00.083 --> 00:03:04.140
and all of those proof-of-concept elements

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.140
have been demonstrated with
the Valkyrie as it's evolved.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.650
And in addition to proving
those basic concepts,

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.480
the Valkyrie's evolved as a system

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.343
so that it can be a
primary platform and system

00:03:15.343 --> 00:03:17.787
that will ultimately be used to perform

00:03:17.787 --> 00:03:19.680
those actual missions.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.990
- [Narrator] The US military
has recently doubled down

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.960
on artificial intelligence
to counter threats from China

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.840
and keep up with its
rapidly expanding arsenal.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.200
- We must move with urgency
and unity of purpose,

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.132
to ensure we can maintain the peace

00:03:33.132 --> 00:03:35.970
and have our troops ready
for whatever may come.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.550
Because that's what's required in this era

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.070
of strategic competition with the PRC.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.720
- [Narrator] While some
military technology

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.210
already incorporates
artificial intelligence,

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.770
like computers that pull data

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.570
from satellite images or video,

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.250
the military is exploring tech

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.320
with much broader capabilities.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.670
From inexpensive drones

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:56.130
with various
intelligence-gathering sensors,

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:58.680
to automated missile defense systems.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:01.830
The military intends to use
these in such large numbers

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:04.230
that enemies can't destroy them all.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:05.063
At this point,

00:04:05.063 --> 00:04:07.980
multiple branches of the
military and defense contractors

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.200
are working on AI pilot systems.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.750
And they're testing
some with the Valkyrie.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.840
The Air Force Research Lab
conducted its first test mission

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.360
with an AI-equipped
Valkyrie over the summer.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.180
And Shield AI, a contractor
for the Defense Department,

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:24.120
is working on its own
AI pilot with the drone.

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.730
The Valkyrie is designed to
run a variety of missions

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.380
in contested airspace.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:31.380
Its AI pilot would use a
range of sensors to monitor

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.180
and interpret its surroundings.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:36.450
The AI would share that
information and act on it,

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.540
issuing commands to the plane's
onboard computer system,

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.100
which would determine the flight path

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.290
and settings to get where it needs to go.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.120
If the Valkyrie locates a target,

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.860
it would get human authorization

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.370
before neutralizing it using
bombs or other weapons.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:51.750
In a military operation,

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.390
the Valkyrie could execute
missions autonomously,

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.910
or be used in conjunction
with fighter jets.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:58.453
Because the Valkyrie can carry up to

00:04:58.453 --> 00:05:00.540
1,800 pounds of payload,

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.870
it could also be used to
launch a variety of weapons.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.300
But many military experts
have voiced concerns

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.640
about putting weapons in
the wings of drones running

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.260
on artificial intelligence.

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.930
That drones could
inadvertently deploy weapons

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.720
that could cause harm
or escalate conflict.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:16.740
- There are huge ethical

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:19.080
and potentially legal
considerations associated

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.350
with putting true artificial
intelligence in a drone.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:23.640
In the United Nations,

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:26.310
there's discussions about
banning lethal autonomous weapons

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.800
of course, but the
problem with all of this

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.200
is that our adversaries
are unlikely to participate

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.050
in any kind of ban on
lethal autonomous weapons.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.520
And the United States, in fact,

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.680
is not participating in any kind of ban.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:41.280
So the real issue is that
even though we choose to act

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:44.400
in a way that conforms with our values

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:47.280
and our role in the international system,

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.560
other countries may not choose to do that.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:52.680
- [Narrator] The Valkyrie is
priced at five to $10 million.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.590
That's a fraction of the
price of a crewed aircraft.

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:59.040
An F-35 fighter jet can
cost about $90 million.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.010
Though in practice, many
cost significantly more.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:05.580
But as the US military looks
to add thousands of AI drones

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.560
within the next two years to its fleet,

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:09.270
it will also be exploring systems

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.040
that are substantially cheaper.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.770
Even if they don't travel
as far, or as fast,

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.330
or carry as many weapons,

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:18.960
they could use the same AI
piloting software being developed

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:20.940
on the XQ-58A.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:23.700
- Other drones could accept
some of the same autonomy.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:27.069
The basic AI and the ability to deploy AI

00:06:27.069 --> 00:06:29.610
across a number of
systems is very important.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:30.960
And if you look at some of the things

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:33.210
that the Air Force has published lately,

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.043
they've been very open.

00:06:34.043 --> 00:06:38.073
Their intent is to have a family
of systems across the DoD,

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:43.710
and to maximize commonality
from an AI perspective,

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.210
from an interface perspective,

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.684
with those different
un-crewed aircraft systems

00:06:48.684 --> 00:06:52.590
so that it doesn't require
one specific trained operator

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.480
for any one aircraft type.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:57.600
The difference again becomes
in the mission capability.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.910
- [Narrator] There's still
development work to go.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.380
In a test mission this summer,

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.030
the Air Force Research Lab said

00:07:03.030 --> 00:07:06.540
an AI-equipped Valkyrie solved
a tactical challenge problem

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:09.330
in the air, but didn't
provide more specifics.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.340
But whether the Valkyrie will move forward

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:12.600
through proposed initiatives

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.010
like the Air Force's planned

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:17.820
collaborative combat aircraft
program remains to be seen.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:20.430
Other companies are also
working on their own drones,

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:23.460
like Boeing's MQ-28 Ghost Bat.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:24.540
According to Kratos,

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.450
the Valkyrie is already at a
stage where it could be used.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:30.930
But full deployment is
probably at least a year away.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.190
- Because the Department of Defense

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:34.710
hasn't really settled on
exactly the types of drones

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:35.550
it wants to buy yet,

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:38.760
and in fact probably
needs a family of drones.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:41.190
What you've seen is that
industry has responded

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.280
to this demand signal with
this wonderfully diverse set

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.010
of capabilities that really
do span the whole spectrum,

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.350
from a very small to the much larger.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:50.310
Some of them are focused on

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:52.170
intelligent surveillance reconnaissance,

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:54.180
some of them can carry
air-to-air missiles.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.880
A real question and the thing
that industry is waiting for

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.490
is where is that demand signal now

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:01.650
to scale production of these drones?

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.030
This is an urgent question

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:07.140
because we want to shore up
for structure in short order

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:09.300
to build up that combat credible force.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.860
- [Narrator] Given how big a shift

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:13.380
economical AI-equipped weapons represent

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.700
for the US military,

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.580
it's unclear exactly
how or when the Valkyrie

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.320
or the software being built on it

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:21.421
will actually reach the battlefield.

00:08:21.421 --> 00:08:24.004
(bright music)

